  "notes": "Stated configuration, not a fixed chassis figure: the E6608 has 6 service-board slots in the DC chassis and 4 in the AC chassis, so \"6x B1LDCD\" is what the port list means. An AC-powered E6608 holds two fewer boards and is a different box - model it separately rather than reusing this one.\n\nThe cages and the fabric are not the same limit. Six B1LDCD boards present 12 line cages, but the OTN cross-connect is 800 Gbit/s (400G packet, 800G OSU) per subrack, so at most 4x 200G of line capacity - or 8x 100GE of client - can actually be mapped at once. The ports are modelled because they physically exist; the 800G bound is the thing to check before planning a fill, and it is why a fully-loaded E6608 is not a 2.4T box.\n\nLine side ports are CFP2 cages and take CFP2 optics only: a 200G QSFP56 module carries the same rate and will not seat, which the link validator refuses by name (E_CONNECTOR_MISMATCH). Order CFP2 optics. Line rates span 1.25G to 400G and the board set includes SFP/eSFP, XFP/TXFP, SFP+/TSFP+, QSFP+, QSFP28 and SFP28 client cages, so a different board mix is a different spec.\n\nNo L2/L3 forwarding: packet switching here is MPLS-TP/pseudowire inside the OTN fabric, so capabilities is cli only - same reading as the Cisco NCS 1004. Protection (client 1+1, ODUk SNCP, LAG/ERPS, SNCP/MSP) and sync (1588v2, G.8275.1) are platform features and are not modelled as port capabilities."
